Rethink exceptions strategy
Improve cabalization

Think of high-level combinators from abstract data types like

class Instrument
data Bond = Bond ... | FixedRateBond ... | FloatingRateBond ...
instance Instrument Bond

data PricingEngine = Engine1 ... | Engine2 ...

data Result = Result{npv :: Double, ...}
calculate :: Instrument -> PricingEngine -> IO Result

While building components for pricing, we will construct contents.
Actual instantiation of QuantLib object will happen inly on pricing.
This allows for easy building of mutators as simply returning a new copy with
updated data

Use some type magic to restrict dates and enforce the same length of dates and amounts for cash flows
(for now the latter is solved by using a list of tuples)

C ENUMERATIONS into Haskell?

